user guide names PhotoCraft's channels or the default branch (rewrite by hand): docs/user/faq/replace-photoshop.md:12: What PhotoCraft does well already: layers, masks, adjustment layers, layer styles, type, vector shapes, brushes and live-preview filters, in a menu and shortcut layout that follows Photoshop. See [PhotoCraft](../index.md) for an overview, and the [project roadmap](https://github.com/storytold/photocraft/blob/main/ROADMAP.md) for what comes next.
user guide names PhotoCraft's channels or the default branch (rewrite by hand): docs/user/getting-started/install.md:3: description: Download PhotoCraft for Windows 10 or 11, macOS or Linux from getartcraft.com or GitHub, or install it with ArtCraft Launcher.
user guide names PhotoCraft's channels or the default branch (rewrite by hand): docs/user/getting-started/install.md:8: The easiest way is the [PhotoCraft page on getartcraft.com](https://getartcraft.com/apps/photocraft). You can also install it with [ArtCraft Launcher](https://getartcraft.com/docs/craft-launcher/guides/install-and-update-apps), which lists PhotoCraft. For a specific build or file format, take it from the [latest release](https://github.com/storytold/photocraft/releases/latest) on GitHub. In the file names below, `<version>` stands for the version number, for example `0.8.2`.
user guide names PhotoCraft's channels or the default branch (rewrite by hand): docs/user/getting-started/install.md:14: 1. Open the [latest release](https://github.com/storytold/photocraft/releases/latest).
user guide names PhotoCraft's channels or the default branch (rewrite by hand): docs/user/index.md:21: PhotoCraft is one of the Crafting Apps from the ArtCraft team, next to VectorCraft, FilmCraft and the other Craft apps. You can install and update them from [ArtCraft Launcher](https://getartcraft.com/docs/craft-launcher).
user guide names PhotoCraft's channels or the default branch (rewrite by hand): docs/user/index.md:25: Ask in [Discord](https://discord.gg/artcraft) or open an issue in the [issue tracker](https://github.com/storytold/photocraft/issues). In PhotoCraft, **Help › Report an Issue…** opens the same issue tracker.
user guide names PhotoCraft's channels or the default branch (rewrite by hand): docs/user/troubleshooting/get-help.md:8: Open **Help › Report an Issue…**. It takes you to the [PhotoCraft issue tracker](https://github.com/storytold/photocraft/issues) on GitHub. You can also ask in [Discord](https://discord.gg/artcraft).
user guide names PhotoCraft's channels or the default branch (rewrite by hand): docs/user/troubleshooting/taskbar-turns-black.md:18: 2. If it is older than 0.8.2, download the [latest release](https://github.com/storytold/photocraft/releases/latest) or update with [ArtCraft Launcher](https://getartcraft.com/docs/craft-launcher). See [Install PhotoCraft](../getting-started/install.md).
user guide names PhotoCraft's channels or the default branch (rewrite by hand): docs/user/troubleshooting/taskbar-turns-black.md:25: PhotoCraft draws its own title bar. When such a window was maximized, Windows sized it to cover the whole screen, taskbar included, took it for a full-screen app and dropped the taskbar's background. The fix keeps a maximized PhotoCraft window clear of the taskbar ([issue 3144](https://github.com/storytold/photocraft/issues/3144), [pull request 3308](https://github.com/storytold/photocraft/pull/3308)).
user guide names PhotoCraft's channels or the default branch (rewrite by hand): docs/user/troubleshooting/taskbar-turns-black.md:29: If you still see it on 0.8.2, add your Windows version and PhotoCraft version to [issue 3864](https://github.com/storytold/photocraft/issues/3864), or ask in [Discord](https://discord.gg/artcraft). As a test, you can switch on **System title bar** under **Edit › Preferences › Interface…**, click **Apply** and restart PhotoCraft; Windows then draws the title bar. See [Get help with a problem](get-help.md) for what to include.
user guide names PhotoCraft's channels or the default branch (rewrite by hand): docs/user/troubleshooting/text-moves-when-editing.md:18: 1. Check your version with **Help › System Info…**. If it is older than 0.8.2, download the [latest release](https://github.com/storytold/photocraft/releases/latest) or update with [ArtCraft Launcher](https://getartcraft.com/docs/craft-launcher).
user guide names PhotoCraft's channels or the default branch (rewrite by hand): docs/user/troubleshooting/text-moves-when-editing.md:25: Clicking a PSD text layer with the Type tool starts editing it, and PhotoCraft then lays the text out itself instead of showing the pixels Photoshop saved. PhotoCraft 0.7.0 read the alignment and size of each run of text only from Photoshop's default styles, and ignored part of the text position that recent Photoshop versions store. Both are fixed in 0.8.2 ([issue 3795](https://github.com/storytold/photocraft/issues/3795), [pull request 3819](https://github.com/storytold/photocraft/pull/3819)).
user guide names PhotoCraft's channels or the default branch (rewrite by hand): docs/user/troubleshooting/text-moves-when-editing.md:29: If text still moves in 0.8.2, keep a copy of the original with **File › Save a Copy…**, then report it in the [issue tracker](https://github.com/storytold/photocraft/issues) with the PSD (zipped) and the Photoshop version that saved it. You can also ask in [Discord](https://discord.gg/artcraft). See [Get help with a problem](get-help.md).
